<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90767" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόχνῠ</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>utterly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥς κε . . ἀπόλωνται π. κακῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.460
				</span></i>
			; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλέσθαι π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.69
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>with the knees forward</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π.
				καθεζομένη</span>, i.e. kneeling or crouching, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.570
			</span></i> (where <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πρόγνυ</span> shd.
			perh. be restd., cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνύπετος</span>, Skt.
				Adj.
			<i>prajñú-</i> (dub. sens.)). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> dub. sens. in Antim.Col.<i><span class="en">
				2P.
			</span></i>: later, simply 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάνυ</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.1118
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.249
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
